Subject: [PATCH] Recordings list: actions where expected, select several, readable names, simpler navigation

The row menu and right-click menu get Transcribe (or Transcribe again), Summarize and Create document.
The preview's empty transcript offers Transcribe in place (the dialog opens there), and greyed-out AI
buttons say why (no transcript yet, or no usable model for chat, with a link to Settings). Several
recordings can be selected (Select mode, Ctrl-click, Shift-click) to transcribe, summarize, add to a
collection or move to Trash together; the Delete key moves the selection (or the open recording) to
Trash and Escape clears it. Trash gets Empty Trash. Recordings still named by their Plaud session
number ("Plaud 1795000000") show when they were recorded instead, in the list, preview, recording
page, Transcripts and AI Chat; this is display only, file names and titles are unchanged. The
Transcripts preview keeps speaker labels. The sidebar has one Recordings entry (Home showed the same
list), grouped under Library and Sources; API & MCP moves to Settings and the footer.
